<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<osm version="0.6" generator="hand-written for the pykci tests">
  <!--
    A hand-made OpenStreetMap extract around the one building of the FZK-Haus LoD2 model
    (input/citygml/FZK-Haus/FZK-Haus-LoD2-KIT-IAI-KHH-B36-V1.gml), the input of
    tests/integration/test_osm_fusion.py. Not real OSM data.

    The building footprint (its GroundSurface) is the rectangle E 457842..457854, N 5439083..5439093
    in EPSG:25832 (12 m x 10 m, 120 m2). Every position below is given in that CRS in the comment
    and was converted to WGS84 with pyproj (7 decimals, about 1 cm), so the reprojected values in
    the graph differ from the round numbers by a centimetre at most.

    With the default clip buffer of 10 m the ingest reads E 457832..457864, N 5439073..5439103.

      way 1001        building, covers the footprint almost fully (shifted 0.5 m east, 0.3 m north):
                      intersection 11.5 x 9.7 = 111.55 m2, overlap ratio 0.93, Jaccard 0.87
      way 1002        building, touches the north-east corner only: intersection 1 x 3 = 3 m2 of its
                      36 m2, overlap ratio 0.083 (below the default threshold 0.3)
      relation 1001   multipolygon building with a courtyard (outer way 1003, inner way 1004), west
                      of the house; the same number as way 1001 on purpose
      way 1004        the courtyard, also a feature of its own (leisure=garden: no kind of its own)
      way 1005        a street south of the house (line)
      way 1006        a fence (line outside the transport and water network: not read)
      way 1007        landuse north of the house
      way 1008        a pond east of the house
      way 1009        scrub west of the house
      way 1010        a building 136 m east: outside every clip window used by the tests
      node 2001       a cafe inside the footprint, 3.61 m from its centre
      node 2002       a bakery outside the footprint
      node 2003       a tree
      node 2004       a bench 30 m east of the house: read with a buffer of 50 m, not with 10 m

    Way 1001 has a tag with a quote and a backslash (the text form GDAL hands tags over in), and
    the tags source (way 1001) and ele (node 2003), which GDAL's default osmconf.ini ignores.
  -->
